 "guidelines": "Every Module II teaching page in PSYC301 collections 09 to 13 is rewritten as a natural teaching transcript that reads aloud like a professor explaining the material. Bullets hold two to five complete, connected sentences and sub-bullets hold one to three. Each page explains what a concept is, how it works and why it matters, in source order, using only source material. There are no fragments, compressed shorthand, report labels, presentation narration, colons, semicolons, dashes, equals signs or arrows in the prose. Title and divider pages stay empty. Earlier editions are not rewritten.",
